Web Accessibility Standards (WCAG 2.1) 
Web accessibility means making websites easy to use for 
everyone, including people with disabilities. 
5 Key Requirements 
1. Readable Text – Use clear fonts, suitable sizes, and readable text. 
2. Alternative Text – Add meaningful alt text to images so screen 
readers can describe them. 
3. Good Color Contrast – Make sure text and background have 
enough contrast for easy reading. 
4. Keyboard Navigation – All important website functions should be 
usable with a keyboard. 
5. Clear Labels and Headings – Use clear headings, labels, and 
instructions so users can understand and navigate the website 
easily. 
Conclusion 
Following WCAG 2.1 accessibility practices makes websites more 
usable, inclusive, and easier to navigate for everyone